    "afterSkip": {
      "id": "",
      "tag": "BODY",
      "text": "Skip to main content\n    \n    \n    \n      WorktreeSecret Broker\n      DemoInstallPrivacy\n    \n    \n    \n      \n        Local CLI · v0.1.0\n        Lease secrets to one worktree process\n        For developers running coding agents, each worktree gets only approved development variables.\n        Try it with sample dataOpens an isolated recorded CLI run.\n        Only approved variables enter the child.Receipts list names, never values.Production labels are denied by default.\n      \n      Only approved variables reach the named worktree process.\n    \n    \n      Sample names-only receiptThe receipt shows names, never valuesThe recording uses the demo’s two bundled names.\n      \n  \n    wsb demo · isolated sample00:00:01\n    $ wsb demo\nDemo — sample data, nothing is saved\nTemporary worktree: /tmp/wsb-demo-4821\nApproved: DATABASE_URL, NPM_TOKEN\nLease: 15 minutes → sample check\n✓ child received 2 approved variable names\nReceipt demo-1787913600\n  worktree: /tmp/wsb-demo-4821\n  names: DATABASE_URL, NPM_TOKEN\n  started: 1787913600\n  expires: 1787914500\n  outcome: demo-complete\n  revoked: 1787913601\nTemporary worktree removed.\n    \n  \n    \n    \n      How it worksRun one worktree process in three steps\n      \n        01Map approved namesPoint each variable name at Keychain, Secret Service, or 1Password.DATABASE_URL → keychain://my-app/database-url\n        02Name the worktreeThe broker checks the Git root before starting one child process.wsb run --worktree ../agent-42 -- npm test\n        03Read the receiptExpiry stops the child. The receipt lists names, timing, and outcome.outcome: child-exited · names: NPM_TOKEN\n      \n      cargo install --git https://github.com/B-Divyesh/sf-worktree-secret-broker.git --lockedView source (external site)Copy install command\n    \n    \n      A narrow toolWhat the broker does not do\n      It does not host a vault.It does not scan repositories.It denies production-labelled entries by default.It cannot hide variables from the child that needs them.\n    \n    \n    Local policy helperGenerate a names-only team policyEnter variable names. The helper creates development-only provider references in this browser.\n    \n      Approved variable names DATABASE_URL\nNPM_TOKENProvider OS keychain1PasswordLease length 5 minutes15 minutes30 minutes60 minutes\n      Generate team policyYour names-only config will appear here.\n    \n  \n  \n    \n      Temporary secret leases for worktree processes.\n      PrivacyTermsBuilt by Param Factory (external site)\n      Version 0.1.0 · build 2026.08.29"
    },
